-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/QHU> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Holocene deposits."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-03-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CARB> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Subsidiary conglomerate and trace mafic igneous-rock, mudstone, sandstone and siltstone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Carboniferous Period (359.3-298.9 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CRET> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Limestone and sandstone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Cretaceous Period (143.1-66 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DEV> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Conglomerate, limestone and mudstone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/JURA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Limestone and mudstone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Jurassic Period (201.4-143.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/JURM> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Calcareous sandstone and limestone with subsidiary sandy limestone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Mid Jurassic Epoch (Jurassic Period) (174.7-161.5 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/KU> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Limestone, sandstone and sedimentary rock based on grain size or crystal size and trace siliceous limestone. Bedrock. Occurs both onshore and offshore. Formed during the Late Cretaceous Epoch (Cretaceous Period) (100.5-66 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PUND> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sandstone with subsidiary breccia and trace mafic igneous-rock. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Permian Period (298.9-251.9 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/TRIA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Conglomerate, mudstone and pebbly (gravelly) sandstone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Triassic Period (251.9-201.4 Ma BP)."@en .
